---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article','headline':'HOA Software Implementation Checklist','mainEntityOfPage':'https://camvella.com/guides/hoa-software-implementation-checklist/','author':{'@type':'Organization','name':'Camvella','url':'https://camvella.com/'},'publisher':{'@type':'Organization','name':'Camvella','url':'https://camvella.com/','logo':{'@type':'ImageObject','url':'https://camvella.com/brand/camvella-logo-stacked.svg'}},'datePublished':'2026-09-10','dateModified':'2026-09-10','inLanguage':'en-US','about':['HOA software implementation','community association software migration']}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="HOA Software Implementation Checklist | Camvella"
  description="A practical implementation checklist for HOA management companies moving communities, accounting, permissions, boards, residents and workflows into new software."
  schema={schema}
>
<section class="guide-hero"><div class="container container--narrow"><p class="section__label">Implementation guide</p><h1>HOA software implementation checklist for a clean cutover.</h1><p>Use this checklist before moving a management portfolio into a new platform so accounting, data, permissions and day-to-day operations do not get separated during transition.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow guide-body">
  <h2>Portfolio and data inventory</h2>
  <ul><li>List every association, unit and property record.</li><li>Confirm owner and resident contact data.</li><li>Inventory documents, violation history, ARC records, vendor files and open work orders.</li><li>Define which history must be migrated versus archived.</li></ul>
  <h2>Accounting cutover</h2>
  <ul><li>Choose the accounting cutoff date.</li><li>Reconcile opening balances before import.</li><li>Map chart-of-accounts structure and funds.</li><li>Validate open AR, AP, budgets and bank balances after migration.</li></ul>
  <h2>Roles and permissions</h2>
  <ul><li>Map managers, accounting staff, board users and support roles.</li><li>Verify association-level data isolation.</li><li>Test who can approve, edit, export and view financial records.</li></ul>
  <h2>Resident and board rollout</h2>
  <ul><li>Prepare portal invitations and login instructions.</li><li>Choose a small pilot group before portfolio-wide launch.</li><li>Confirm support ownership for first-week questions.</li></ul>
  <h2>Go-live verification</h2>
  <ul><li>Run one violation, ARC request, work order and accounting workflow end to end.</li><li>Verify email and SMS delivery.</li><li>Confirm reports, documents and audit history.</li><li>Keep a rollback/export copy of pre-cutover data.</li></ul>
  <p class="guide-related"><strong>Planning the purchase first?</strong> Read the <a href="/guides/hoa-software-buyers-guide">HOA software buyer’s guide</a> and <a href="/guides/hoa-software-pricing-guide">pricing guide</a>.</p>
  <div class="guide-cta"><h2>See how Camvella handles implementation.</h2><p>We can walk through your current stack, portfolio size and migration priorities in a product demo.</p><a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/demo">Book a Demo</a><a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/guides/hoa-software-buyers-guide">Read the Buyer’s Guide</a></div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
